      {
        "id": 8933990,
        "name": "Abcreator",
        "username": "Abcreator",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/abcreator/{size}/8462529_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-05-11T17:38:58.788Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ScipioAfrikanos\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"2324412\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/scipioafrikanos/60/5813106_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ScipioAfrikanos:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We don’t advise you build any workflows on top of this behavior</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’m sorry however how are we reasonably supposed to test teleporting a group of players if teleporting multiple players is disallowed on the same machine and Studio teleporting is non-existent! I can’t possibly be expected as a Roblox developer to have multiple devices lying around to simply test my own experience’s systems, I hope this functionality is added in the future since as of currently it just ends up damaging developer UX as I can no longer test multiplayer in my game by myself <img src=\"https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/images/emoji/twitter/frowning.png?v=12\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
